{"title":"2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part D","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An <i>arithmetic sequence</i> is a sequence in which each term after the first is obtained from the previous term by adding a constant. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/b/18b109bbad8ddff023f591be8a7ed806fdcc5938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5, 7, 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> is an arithmetic sequence with three terms.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_D&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/5/115991d3aca97f472a93f59a5d4ebdaea8ae4423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y - 6), (2y + 3), (y^{2} + 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"200\" height=\"21\" />, in that order, form an arithmetic sequence with three terms. Determine all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_D&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the difference between consecutive terms stays the same in an arithmetic sequence:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68ab90eb21b618d48eca24806d3a12e136cd22a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2y + 3) - (y - 6) = (y^{2} + 2) - (2y + 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"316\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/1/da1c735e4df842ef0214052a7feba40ea76e5cd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y + 9 = y^{2} - 2y - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/3/223e75cf33f479b1440943fcbed0eb0ebde54d37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^{2} - 3y - 10 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/7/b074830f05d7d2ed47f4e110e1d02388e24c4600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 - 2 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/6/6a6e5f37861d1d64b0a6afdd09ab2fad7644680a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 2 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/0/430a5589c2079f6dd31f50042d928110874c3ee0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^{2} - 5y + 2y - 10 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6eb8e74ad5c1865e6f1957efca608d744f031c92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y(y - 5) + 2(y - 5) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"186\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/0/d3029356c1a8808f0242d16407b1baa52ef36f11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y - 5)(y + 2) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>The possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> would be either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/9/889f56ce08684be3b2ab9914892de17686ae9594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, then the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/a/17abe71ae85115c8f655cd093a1d57d81ebc3fca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 - 6 = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" />, the second term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/e/8ee00216b3b684a747d11677855edac2717fc922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 5 + 3 = 10 + 3 = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"190\" height=\"15\" />, and the third term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/9/ec97cec1c89d0d0a9ed1b496788c5fd90e5fce34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{2} + 2 = 25 + 2 = 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" />. The common difference is still <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7ee09b4a80f3cbe958002dcd6a9942d00ba0bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 - (-1) = 27 - 13 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"20\" />, so this is an arithmetic sequence. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/4/cd4e4527536cb210f5359c8e421f72aa92f215b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{y = 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"29\" /> is a valid solution.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/d/9fd395e96b1e4558dd201a3db8f41306bcbab938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />, then the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/d/39dc4a3fea802fee9c7d0d9fcaba540c4755d2b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2 - 6 = -8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />, the second term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa20f0f1b9e2e98ff8296b550f7507a1422037a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times -2 + 3 = -4 + 3 = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"214\" height=\"15\" />, and the third term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/0925cdfb7dbafe1138febca2d01986123a39000c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-2)^{2} + 2 = 4 + 2 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"176\" height=\"21\" />. The common difference is still <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/883e6126966263d16d3856485edcf6ad40c6fa10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1 - (-8) = 6 - (-1) = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"211\" height=\"20\" />, so this is an arithmetic sequence. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/7/a57d14b45a7eb99cc7aa3aa98c2d37b97dcf9cb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{y = -2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"70\" height=\"29\" /> is a valid solution.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018060317\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.034 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 92/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 302/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4862/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.868      1 2014_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\n100.00%    6.868      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37230:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018060317 and revision id 287509. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}